# CLAUDE.md is loaded into context at the start of every session, so its size is
# a running cost rather than a one-off. `docs(claude-md): unpad the monorepo
# table` (7ef9d531) deliberately stripped the alignment padding from its tables
# for that reason -- and column padding is precisely what prettier's markdown
# printer insists on adding back: 126 lines of pure whitespace across the
# package and route tables, which buys no legibility in a file that is read by a
# model far more often than by a person.
#
# Same call as the wire golden above, for the same reason: the shape of this
# content is owned by what consumes it, not by the formatter.
#
# How this surfaced, since it is worth not repeating: 7ef9d531 was a docs-only
# push, so `detect-changes` skipped `lint-and-typecheck` and `format:check`
# never ran on it. main sat red for that check while every main run reported
# green, until the next PR touching code (WXYC/Backend-Service#2670) ran the job
# and failed on a file it had not touched.
#
# Consequence to know: prettier no longer normalizes ANYTHING in this file, so
# list markers, code fences and table pipes are on author discipline here.
CLAUDE.md
